{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975990866,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc97848ffe0WlvSbtl03avaE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_VJY67KBydAxTsDFTQkari8XF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n@@\n ‘Betz cell’ subClassOf ‘has characteristic’ some ‘standard pyramidal morphology’\n+\n+### Recording epithelial cell shape\n+\n+For epithelial cell types whose definition depends on shape, record the\n+shape using [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+with a PATO morphology term. This applies both to named epithelial shape\n+classes and to more specific epithelial cell types whose name or definition\n+states the shape.\n+\n+For example, [squamous epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000076)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [flattened](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002254).\n+\n+For example, [cuboidal epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_9900000)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [cuboid](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001872).\n \n ### Recording nuclear number \n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM docs/relations_guide.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n@@ -234,8 +234,26 @@\n neuronal), e.g.\n \n ‘Betz cell’ subClassOf ‘has characteristic’ some ‘standard pyramidal morphology’\n \n+### Recording epithelial cell shape\n+\n+For epithelial cell types whose definition depends on shape, record the\n+shape using [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+with a PATO morphology term. This applies both to named epithelial shape\n+classes and to more specific epithelial cell types whose name or definition\n+states the shape.\n+\n+For example, [squamous epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000076)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [flattened](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002254).\n+\n+For example, [cuboidal epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_9900000)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [cuboid](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001872).\n+\n ### Recording nuclear number \n \n To record the number of nuclei in a cell, use a PATO subclass\n under the term ['nucleate quality'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001404) with the ['has\n@@ -258,5 +276,4 @@\n ## Taxon constraints\n \n See\n <https://oboacademy.github.io/obook/explanation/taxon-constraints-explainer/>.\n-\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md","relativePath":"docs/relations_guide.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md\n@@ -234,8 +234,26 @@\n neuronal), e.g.\n \n ‘Betz cell’ subClassOf ‘has characteristic’ some ‘standard pyramidal morphology’\n \n+### Recording epithelial cell shape\n+\n+For epithelial cell types whose definition depends on shape, record the\n+shape using [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+with a PATO morphology term. This applies both to named epithelial shape\n+classes and to more specific epithelial cell types whose name or definition\n+states the shape.\n+\n+For example, [squamous epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000076)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [flattened](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002254).\n+\n+For example, [cuboidal epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_9900000)\n+is equivalent to [epithelial cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000066)\n+and [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n+*some* [cuboid](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001872).\n+\n ### Recording nuclear number \n \n To record the number of nuclei in a cell, use a PATO subclass\n under the term ['nucleate quality'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001404) with the ['has\n@@ -258,5 +276,4 @@\n ## Taxon constraints\n \n See\n <https://oboacademy.github.io/obook/explanation/taxon-constraints-explainer/>.\n-\n","additions":18,"deletions":1}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM docs/relations_guide.md","time":{"start":1778975990852,"end":1778975990864}},"id":"prt_e333b493e0016HhJxg9BwxRfSs","sessionID":"ses_1ccc97848ffe0WlvSbtl03avaE","messageID":"msg_e333b3c8f0012GdQC49rX3QIDv"}}
